// ---------------------------------------------------------------- crossbow bolt: lodged in the shoulder, bleeding, pulled out by hand
// Every crossbow hit lodges a bolt in the shoulder, forces bleeding, never knocks the victim down; pulling the bolt out (TLOU2's
// own pull-out action) is awkward under fire and stops the bleed; left in, it can down them.
// 2013 DATA (re/factions2013/crossbow-2013.md): the crossbow IS a 2013 Factions DLC weapon (net10.bin key 94b0435b = sid32("crossbow"): firearm def,
// damage row 'player' 55, ammo-crossbow item) and its bleed is the 2013 script re/t1ps3/patch1/ss-crossbow.bin (ss-multiplayer/ss-crossbow.dc):
// a hit by the crossbow on a living player starts timer-bleed-out at 0.24 s; every tick takes 1 hp (set-player-health(hp - 1)); at hp 1 the player is
// DOWNED (credited to the crossbow attacker) unless they are holding the heal command; healing to full (health kit) or a teammate's heal stops it,
// as does dying / respawning. There is NO pull-out in 2013 (the pull-out hold below is OUR addition, kept: the bleed pauses while pulling).
// So XB_TICK_MS 240 / XB_TICK_HP 1 are 2013's; the shot is NOT floored (a 55 hit that downs normally downs, no bolt / bleed then - the script needs health > 0).
// The rule kept from 2013: a gun / bow hit never kills a standing player, bleed only DOWNS (downed_set(1), the normal 2013 downed pool + bleed-out).
// TLOU2 SP system found (exe + DC, Ghidra / dconstruct): the player's arrow-stuck state lives in C++ (player + 0x3218 controller:
// vfunc +0x178 = player-is-arrow-stuck?, +0x1a8 = player-get-arrow-stuck-meter; state callbacks at exe 0x140af4b70 / 0x140af51a0 / 0x140af7320
// that send the events player-arrow-stuck / player-arrow-removed to the HUD script ss-hud2-arrow-status-prompt), the pull-out input is the
// joypad command remove-arrow-hold (HUD script polls joypad-command-active?(remove-arrow-hold, 6)), the stuck-hit reactions are
// *player-arrow-stuck-reaction-list* (ellie-fb-hr-arrow-knockdown-stand-*-shldr: a KNOCKDOWN set, used by the engine for a real arrow). No DC
// native sets the stuck state (only getters + break-arrow-stuck-in-player), and the C++ entry is not a callable function we could prove
// blind, so the engine's stuck-arrow visual / pull animation is NOT driven; this block runs the gameplay around the real command + a blood fx.
// ROUND 2 (Ghidra of exe 0x140af2xxx-0x140afaxxx = re/ "player-arrow-pull.cpp", class with states HitReaction-gated ArrowStuck / PullingArrow /
// Ending / Inactive): the entry IS callable. The controller at player+0x3218 has vtable +0x190 = claim-hit (exe 0x140afa310, only for the engine's own
// arrow hits), +0x198 = OnArrowStuck(this, arrowObject, hitRecord) (exe 0x140af69d0: stores the arrow handle at this+0xe0/+0xe8, picks the shoulder
// settings with 0x140af3af0 from the hit record, writes the reaction row into hitRecord+0x140, sends player-arrow-stuck, enters state ArrowStuck),
// +0x1b0 = clear (0x140af4b70: player-arrow-removed event, registry entry dropped). Its gate: byte exe+0x4104a60 (a debug flag) OR (player state ==
// HitReaction && an active reaction) - we set the flag only around our one call. The arrow prop + attach is the DC native spawn-stuck-arrow(entity, joint)
// (exe 0x140428960: a ProjectileArrow spawned at the entity, FUN_14119b1b0 attaches it to the joint and registers it in the stuck-arrow registry that
// get-arrow-stuck-in-character / -in-player read). The KNOCKDOWN list (*player-arrow-stuck-reaction-list*) is only picked by the hit-reaction function
// 0x140cbed90 when AttackInfo+0x9b5 bit 5 is set, which the engine's claim step sets; we never run the claim step and hand the stick call a scratch
// record, so its reaction row lands in scratch memory and nothing falls. Pull-out is the engine's own (remove-arrow-hold -> PullingArrow + its clips +
// HUD), the bolt ends when player-is-arrow-stuck? goes false. If the engine entry does not take (no stuck state within 0.5 s) the custom hold below runs.
#define MSG_XBOLT 0x6E             // peer msg (ours): [u8 state 1 bolt in / 0 out][u8 shoulder 0 left / 1 right] - the victim's keep-alive / clear
#define XB_TICK_MS 580             // measured 6-7 s to the down at 444 ms, +2 s wanted -> 580 ms (~8.5 s)
#define XB_TICK_HP 2               // hp per tick: compromise between 2013 (1 per 0.24 s, ~10.6 s from 45 hp) and our fast one (14 hp/s): 2 per 0.24 s = ~8.3 hp/s, ~5.4 s from 45 hp
#define XB_KEEP_HP 0               // 2013: no floor on the shot (0 = off); the bolt / bleed start only if the shot leaves us alive
#define XB_PULL_MS 2000            // hold remove-arrow-hold this long, unbroken, to pull the bolt (OUR value, 2013 had no pull-out)
#define XB_HIT_BREAK_MS 600        // any hit on us this recently restarts the pull
