                        if (gik < 0) { FILE *gf = exe_side_open("t2r-uc4-gik.txt", "r"); gik = gf != NULL; if (gf) fclose(gf); }   // opt-in: it crashed twice in the anim binding update
                        // No "weight" line at all. The layer update 0x1415f6a20 RAMPS +0x40 by
                        // itself every frame (+-rate, clamped 0..1), so +0x40 is no switch. Its fade is: +0x2c timer
                        // left, +0x30 length, +0x34 start, +0x48 target -> +0x44 = lerp (timer <= 0: +0x44 = +0x48);
                        // effective blend = +0x44 * +0x40. So the fade is pinned to 0 instead (timer 0, start 0,
                        // target 0, current 0) every frame, +0x3d (fading out = release at 0) never set, the state
                        // instance stays for the prone disable. Diag once a second: the layer fields.
