    // we used to stop it a frame later (its first frames + whoosh showed, and every miss of the target test - 70 deg cone, 2.2 m - was a
    // standing swing at the lying body). Now: while a downed enemy is the ONLY target in reach (dm_target; a standing one as close wins) the
    // engine's melee is held off (player-disable-melee every frame, as the 0.75 s lock does) and the press itself - the game's melee command
    // or the F key, read before the engine acts on it - starts the ground attack. t2r-dmelee-no-preempt.txt = the old stop-after-start path only.
    int press_edge = 0, pre = 0, ts_pre = -1, e_blk_frame = 0; float d_pre = 0;
