// ---------------------------------------------------------------- paired-move path gate (an upgraded melee kill let the victim fall through the map)
// Every paired move carries both bodies along the clips' baked root motion with no collider (our own body by the engine's align, a puppet by psync),
// and nothing looked at what is out there: in an A/B test (a log [52768] and a player's report of the same event) the 2013 side swing took both bodies
// ~2.3 m through a chest-high wall 0.46 m behind the victim and left them over a drop - the engine shoved the attacker ~2.5 m in 5 frames
// ('root stepped 0.4-0.9 m'), both fell to y 8.4 / 9.3 and died. Before a pair is begun the clips' END placements (psync_pair_end, from the ap, no move
// needed) are checked in the static world (mask 0x207, kick now / read next frame): a ray from each body's start to its end spot at y+0.7 and y+1.2
// (a hit more than 0.3 m before the end, beyond 0.15 m from the start = a wall / prop in the way) and a ray down at each end spot (a floor within
// 0.5 m of the start height, else a drop / void). Returns 1 = clear (or unknown: rays / clips unreadable, logged), 0 = BLOCKED, 2 = rays kicked, ask
// again next frame (cached per slot + pair ~0.75 s while both bodies stay put). One-shots: BLOCKED = the plain down hit; E executions: another variant /
// no start; shiv: no prompt. t2r-no-upgraded-pathgate.txt next to the exe = off.
static int psync_pair_end(const float *ap7, uint64_t att_sid, uint64_t vic_sid, float ph, int gun, float out[2][8]);   // paired.c
static uint64_t world_ray_kick_ign(const float *a, const float *b, uint64_t obj);
static uint64_t world_ray_kick_m(const float *a, const float *b, uint64_t ign, uint32_t mask);
// Release blocker (you could still melee people into spaces you can't walk out from): EXIT RING. The gates and tails below judged walls ON the
// clip's path and a sealed-in spot (7 of 8 inward rays), never whether a body that ends THERE can walk away: a pocket between a chest-high wall and a
// knee-high shelf base reads 3 of 8 sides blocked. The exit ring casts, from a spot, 8 directions x 3 parallel rays (centre + 0.28 m either side = one capsule
// wide) of EX_LEN at knee height (0.5 m: a 0.45 m shelf base / crate stops a walker) in the static world (0x1b07: grass passes). A direction is PASSABLE when
// all three read clear; a spot with no passable direction has no walkable exit. t2r-no-exit-check.txt next to the exe = off (gates, pair stop, tail).
