// at exe+1b5ec33 is routed to a stub that does what the function's own 'no handle' state is (out handle {0, 0, valid = 1}, as at 0x1b5ed3f), logs once per
// 8 hits, and jumps to the epilogue at 0x1b5edf7: the spawn is refused, the caller gets an empty handle (every caller already handles a failed spawn).
// (2) exe+1b99fe5 (loading the menu stage): data-loading.cpp line 0x356 'pLevel->m_ppLightTables == nullptr' - a level record that already
// carries its light tables is loaded again. The call of the assert handler at exe+1b99f82 becomes a jump to the next record step (0x1b99fef): the second
