// every full-body clip WE force on the local player (the execution carriers, the downed fall npc-nw-idle-hr-stun-bomb-bw, the
// lying / victim halves) is an NPC clip; the engine answers it like any player clip without weapon support - the clip's
// PlayerHolsterWeaponAnimAction begins (the put-away arm layer = the visible sling-to-back move) and ~37 frames in the per-frame
// item update (0x140bd8b80, request at 0xbd91cf) asks for the animated Holster state (logs: shiv 9036 - no gate at all;
// downed 12992 fall -> 13029 "Holster item state request passed ... bd91cf"; gun executions: the same bd91cf request at +37,
// SKIPPED only because hfix_active() covered the armed attacker half). The gates were limited to the armed attacker half: the
// unarmed executions (fists / neck-break / shiv: g_unarm_exec switched every gate off so our own instant holster could pass), the
// victim half and the downed fall / lying had none. hfix_scope() = any of our forced full-body states on the local player; the
// anim-action sources (begin / body / Phase1 / Phase2 / attach events) and the engine's own Holster state requests are refused in
// it, while OUR own weapon calls (holster-player-weapon-instantly, the unarmed draw: a t2r-ext.dll frame on the request's stack)
// still pass. The weapon attach (sling fix) stays limited to the armed attacker half: the instant holster's re-attach must run.
