// holster-fix / sling-fix / bp line fired in that window, so none of our gates was involved and the engine's own re-attach is unseen).
// Every weapon attach whose owner is the local player is logged OUTSIDE our execution halves too (first 400 per process): frame, the
// weapon process (+ whether it is the held one), the attach point sid (hand / holster / back), the caller chain. The next bug clip's
// lines show which caller moved the stowed gun to leftHand (0xf170dca7466d11c1) and in which step of the switch.
// The trace only sees attach calls through 0x141cd2210 / 0x141cd67e0; B 87248 showed the engine stowing the rifle on
// targLongGunSlotOne through them while the gun stayed in the hand on screen, so some later attach is not covered (the instant
// attach 0x141cd2140 / the anim-event attach 0x141cd25a0). Census: every local-player weapon process seen by the trace (and the
// held one) is polled for 10 s afterwards and its attach point sid (0x141cd4870) is logged whenever it CHANGES ("attach census:"),
// with the frame - the line where the gun moves to leftHand (f170dca7466d11c1) / rightHand (784a7089a57078e0) names the step.
