    // animation, then it reappears in the hand (recording +0.8..+1.5 s: the right hand opens flat with the 2x4 across the palm, swings low by the hip, grips it
    // again) = what BeginHolster does (notes above: the weapon overlay -> s_weapon-holster, the put-away ARM clip; it does not re-parent the item) while everything that
    // would really stow the item is refused in a victim half ("stow fix: PlayerHolsterWeaponAnimAction not begun (... victim half)"). The gate covered the attacker
    // half, the finisher windup and our generic reaction (v5-dis3 below: B 36833, the engine's begin-holster from exe+2c4c8d on the reaction's first frame) - not the
    // victim half. Skipped whole there (plain gate, as v5-dis2 / v5-dis3: we never call begin-holster ourselves). Inferred for the victim half, not seen in a log:
