    // the victim's hand-off ends the psync move. Counting that free time as "the move" (both takedowns: the attacker walked
    // 8.5 m away over the low cover he had just used, the knee ray from the pre-move spot hit that cover, and the guard put him back on
    // the start spot at the hand-off = the 8.7 m "teleport to the downed victim", seen on B as 'jitter: slot 0 jumped 8.74 m'). The move
    // ends at the release: the path checked is the one the clip carried us, not where the player walked afterwards.
    int cd_free = psync_role() == 1 && g_ps.kind == PS_CTXDOWN && g_cd_sfx.uid == g_ps.uid && g_cd_sfx.att_rel;
    // (reports of rubberbanding back a few seconds after an execution and of being moved inside walls): EVERY pair kind's
    // attacker half ends at its blend-out back to locomotion (psync_att_out + the clip's drive through the fade), not only ctxdown's. The old
    // window ran to the hand-off / g_gx.until / g_exec_until, i.e. also over the seconds the player was already running: the straight ray from
    // the start spot to the run's end spot crossed the cover he ran round (4.4 m / 7.4 m 'THROUGH GEOMETRY') and he was pulled back. The path
    // guarded is now the one the clip carried the body along; what the player walked after the release is never a move of ours.
    int att_free = psync_role() == 1 && g_ps.kind != PS_CTXDOWN && g_ps.out_done[0] && g_ps.ent_att == SID_PLAYER && psync_ms() > g_ps.att_drive_until;
    if (att_free) cd_free = 1;
